1
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:10,176
Subtitles are color-coded by country,
and this setting cannot be changed.

2
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,220
Ten minutes left.

3
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:14,723
Revealing the interim weight score.

4
00:00:20,478 --> 00:00:21,730
We're the same!

5
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:23,314
We're the same!

6
00:00:26,151 --> 00:00:27,110
Damn.

7
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:31,823
We're 400 each.

8
00:00:32,824 --> 00:00:34,993
We're 400 each. Look, we're 400 each.

9
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:35,910
Let's go.

10
00:00:36,494 --> 00:00:38,997
At that stage,
because it said 400 kilos each,

11
00:00:40,373 --> 00:00:43,626
my mindset was just, "I have to win this."

12
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:46,046
It's 400?

13
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:47,505
We're both 400!

14
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:50,925
The score really threw me off.

15
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:56,097
I worried we hadn't been doing enough.
I was starting to panic.

16
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:01,061
But we're warriors,
and we don't stop until we win.

17
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:05,523
It's rolling backward! Tie it to the post!

18
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:06,691
8 BAGS

19
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,152
I kept pushing,
but it just wouldn't budge.

20
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:14,783
Just then, Orgil came to the rescue.

21
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:17,202
Hey, let me.

22
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:19,579
That's it. Keep going. One, two.

23
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:22,957
My role required more intense activity…

24
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:24,000
ENKH-ORGIL
MMA FIGHTER

25
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:28,755
…carrying and pushing sandbags

26
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:31,925
with explosive power and speed.

27
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:35,929
That's it. Keep going. One, two.

28
00:01:36,012 --> 00:01:37,430
-Keep going. One, two.
-Okay.

29
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:39,098
One, two!

30
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:46,523
Good work, guys!

31
00:01:51,945 --> 00:01:55,949
My focus was just to keep on going.

32
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,119
As long as there was time,

33
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:02,789
I kept going even though I was exhausted.

34
00:02:04,624 --> 00:02:08,294
My knees were really beginning to go,

35
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:12,465
but I still pushed it.

36
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:19,055
Awesome job. Keep going.

37
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:21,474
Low!

38
00:02:23,768 --> 00:02:28,690
The moment I saw the boxes
not arriving towards me,

39
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:31,025
it was disheartening,

40
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:34,612
because I saw
how fast Mongolia was moving,

41
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:39,409
and I still wasn't receiving any crates.

42
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:44,122
I knew the only way that I could help them
was to just use my voice.

43
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:45,415
Keep it up. Great job, Manny.

44
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:47,208
Great job, Mark. Come on, Justin.

45
00:02:47,292 --> 00:02:49,085
Let's go! Good work, guys!

46
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:51,045
Hey! Here!

47
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:54,299
Awesome job. Keep going!

48
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:55,925
Low!

49
00:03:03,641 --> 00:03:05,018
Great work, guys.

50
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:07,896
Good work!

51
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:11,190
I was encouraged when I heard Robyn
cheering and shouting for us,

52
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:13,484
because Justin and I were really dying.

53
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:36,799
I was really out of breath

54
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:40,053
because I went all in
for the first ten minutes.

55
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:45,433
There were a lot of crates,
and it was tough work.

56
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:51,648
Shit!

57
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:56,402
One, two!

58
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:00,615
One! Two!

59
00:04:01,532 --> 00:04:05,119
7 BAGS

60
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:07,538
-One! Two!
-One! Two!

61
00:04:16,714 --> 00:04:19,300
-Climb inside it. Actually, I'll do it.
-Sure.

62
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:23,680
Don't push yourself too hard.

63
00:04:24,806 --> 00:04:28,101
All right. One, two, three, up!

64
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:30,687
-Move it! Let's go!
-Ready?

65
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:32,438
-One, two, three, up!
-One, two, three!

66
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:35,858
One more!

67
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:36,859
Let's go!

68
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:38,695
-One more, Ray, one more!
-One more!

69
00:04:38,778 --> 00:04:40,655
-One, two, three, up!
-One more! Let's go!

70
00:04:40,738 --> 00:04:43,491
Yes! Good work!

71
00:04:43,574 --> 00:04:45,743
Yes! I got the rest, go!

72
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:46,995
Great job, guys.

73
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:07,765
One minute.

74
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:11,811
All right, come on!

75
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,398
One minute, come on.

76
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:17,608
Let's go, Manny!

77
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:20,903
Keep going!

78
00:05:25,325 --> 00:05:26,451
Send it down quickly!

79
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:28,286
Should we go and get more?
We don't have any more!

80
00:05:28,369 --> 00:05:31,122
Send the cart down!

81
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,584
Watch out!

82
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:37,420
Push!

83
00:05:40,506 --> 00:05:42,050
Set, three, go.

84
00:05:52,935 --> 00:05:55,021
-Push! Come on, hurry!
-Ten seconds.

85
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:01,319
Come on!
Everyone, grab one and throw! Quick!

86
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:07,909
Stop.

87
00:06:07,992 --> 00:06:09,035
Game over.

88
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:20,379
That's got to be enough, right?

89
00:06:33,601 --> 00:06:34,685
Nice, brother.

90
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:36,020
-Good work, guys.
-Good work, team.

91
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:37,522
Nice one.

92
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:38,689
Great job, guys.

93
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:47,240
The second quest of Physical: Asia.

94
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:49,617
Shipwreck transportation match.

95
00:06:50,118 --> 00:06:51,661
The result of Mongolia
versus the Philippines

96
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:53,496
will now be announced.

97
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:03,589
The Philippines.

98
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:09,137
Well done.

99
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,389
-Good job, guys.
-1,290 kg.

100
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:17,603
THE PHILIPPINES
3 CRATES, 57 BAGS

101
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:18,813
Mongolia.

102
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:38,458
PHYSICAL: ASIA

103
00:07:41,544 --> 00:07:45,673
4. DESPERATE PRAYER

104
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:47,216
Mongolia.

105
00:07:52,346 --> 00:07:54,182
-Yes!
-2,000 kg.

106
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:07,069
MONGOLIA
20 CRATES, 50 BAGS

107
00:08:14,243 --> 00:08:16,329
Yes, I did my best on that part,

108
00:08:17,121 --> 00:08:18,706
but it still wasn't enough.

109
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:19,832
I feel sorry for that.

110
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:25,421
We were just outsized.
That's what happened.

111
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:31,302
We cannot blame someone or anybody.

112
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:36,098
I'd just like to tell my team
that we did our best.

113
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:38,768
It's hard to accept defeat.

114
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:49,153
We won because we worked as a team,
and everyone nailed their role.

115
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:51,822
We're ready to take on
any challenge that comes our way.

116
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:55,660
-Warriors, mount up!
-Mount up!

117
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:06,045
I think it'll involve…

118
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:07,463
SUPERBON
MUAY THAI FIGHTER

119
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:08,881
…rescuing a shipwrecked vessel.

120
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:10,299
Or dragging it out of the water.

121
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:14,053
-We might even have to dive underwater.
-You never know.

122
00:09:14,136 --> 00:09:15,096
But we just might.

123
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:16,722
If it's swimming, we'd win hands down.

124
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:19,725
I'm actually a merman
who turned into a human.

125
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:23,980
-Let's tie up James and dunk him…
-Well, they're having a blast.

126
00:09:24,063 --> 00:09:25,356
Just say that you want to kill me.

127
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:27,066
They're having fun.

128
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:29,110
We know nothing about the other teams

129
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:31,028
because we were busy
with our matches yesterday.

130
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:32,446
We've got no read on Thailand.

131
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:33,364
-No.
-Right?

132
00:09:33,447 --> 00:09:36,284
-We didn't see them play at all.
-We have no information to work with.

133
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:40,288
I can't size that guy up.

134
00:09:40,371 --> 00:09:41,706
Exactly.

135
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:42,957
He's an unknown factor.

136
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,418
-He could be a total beast.
-Maybe he's crazy strong.

137
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:46,419
Yeah, right?

138
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:48,629
That guy's a wrestler,
so he'll have the strength and skill.

139
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:50,256
Yeah, he's a Greco-Roman wrestler.

140
00:09:50,339 --> 00:09:51,173
JAR
CROSSFIT ATHLETE

141
00:09:51,257 --> 00:09:52,592
I'm curious about that CrossFitter.

142
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:55,469
-She was in the CrossFit Games.
-She must have good stamina then.

143
00:10:03,352 --> 00:10:05,813
They're having a blast over there.

144
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:08,566
They were laughing nonstop.

145
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:09,650
CHOI SEUNG-YEON
CROSSFIT ATHLETE

146
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:11,235
It seemed like they were here on vacation.

147
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:13,070
They didn't seem to be
taking it seriously.

148
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:16,907
People like that are usually
knocked out early.

149
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:20,494
It was all an act.

150
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:25,082
It wasn't that we were
letting our guards down.

151
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:28,210
We were playing it safe so they wouldn't
catch on to our game plan.

152
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:29,795
20 MINUTES AGO

153
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:30,880
I know how we can win.

154
00:10:30,963 --> 00:10:33,007
The way I see it, Korea's weak link

155
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:34,300
is the fat guy.

156
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:37,720
I noticed while watching
yesterday's matches

157
00:10:37,803 --> 00:10:40,640
that he was a lot weaker
than I thought he would be.

158
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:42,433
He couldn't even beat
the small Japanese guy.

159
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:43,684
You're right.

160
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,686
The girls weren't that strong either.

161
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:47,855
I reckon Ploy's stronger than them.

162
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:50,608
They have no idea what we're capable of,

163
00:10:50,691 --> 00:10:52,818
but we've got them figured out,

164
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:56,238
from their strengths to weaknesses.

165
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:58,366
We'll show them we're not some pushovers.

166
00:10:58,866 --> 00:11:00,034
SUN
NATIONAL TEAM RUGBY PLAYER

167
00:11:00,117 --> 00:11:03,746
We've got some unique strengths
we're keeping under wraps until the match.

168
00:11:03,829 --> 00:11:05,539
We're just as ready to fight as they are.

169
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:08,084
On behalf of all of Thailand,

170
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:10,586
we're going to win this, no matter what.

171
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:16,550
I hope they're underestimating us
and getting all cocky.

172
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:20,096
Proving people like them wrong
and making them leave in tears?

173
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:21,097
That's my specialty.

174
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:25,184
I'll be dialed in every second
and give it my absolute everything.

175
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:39,407
This is insane. What's this now?

176
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:40,908
This is incredible.

177
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:46,872
What is this?

178
00:11:48,541 --> 00:11:49,375
This is unreal.

179
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:52,253
It's on a completely different scale
from the last season.

180
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:55,047
Physical: Asia.

181
00:11:56,090 --> 00:12:00,219
The second quest that will determine
the first countries to be eliminated is

182
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:03,472
the shipwreck transportation match.

183
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:06,934
I'm at a loss for words.

184
00:12:07,601 --> 00:12:08,686
This is wild.

185
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:12,398
This is crazy. Absolutely crazy.

186
00:12:12,481 --> 00:12:13,941
Look at how massive it is.

187
00:12:14,024 --> 00:12:16,777
It's like we're in Universal Studios.

188
00:12:18,070 --> 00:12:19,321
-Okay.
-Okay.

189
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:21,699
-This is about stamina.
-It is.

190
00:12:22,491 --> 00:12:23,868
Objectively, we have the upper hand

191
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:26,078
in both strength and stamina
over Team Thailand.

192
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:27,121
KIM DONG-HYUN
MMA FIGHTER

193
00:12:27,204 --> 00:12:31,459
I believed this was probably the quest
that best played to our strengths.

194
00:12:32,042 --> 00:12:34,295
I think this will be fun.

195
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:35,921
SUPERBON
MUAY THAI FIGHTER

196
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:39,467
It's something I've never done before,
so I'm excited to give it a go.

197
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:41,010
-Let's do this.
-Let's go!

198
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:41,927
Bring it in, everyone.

199
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:44,555
Republic of Korea!

200
00:12:44,638 --> 00:12:45,723
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

201
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:47,057
Let's do this.

202
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:48,601
Let's have fun with this.

203
00:12:48,684 --> 00:12:50,394
Let's go, Thailand!

204
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:51,520
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

205
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:57,109
The second quest of Physical: Asia.

206
00:12:57,735 --> 00:13:00,029
-Let's go!
-Shipwreck transportation match.

207
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:01,947
-Get ready, guys.
-The game between

208
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:04,241
the Republic of Korea
and Thailand will now begin.

209
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:06,785
Stand by.

210
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:07,745
Bring it on.

211
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:09,872
Get ready to roll, guys.

212
00:13:09,955 --> 00:13:11,290
-Ready…
-Let's go.

213
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:13,042
We'll work as a team

214
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:15,044
and show them we're in a different league.

215
00:13:17,421 --> 00:13:19,215
I can guarantee we'll win this.

216
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:20,716
Ready.

217
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,969
-Come on.
-Go, go!

218
00:13:36,774 --> 00:13:38,234
Oh, this is metal.

219
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:39,193
Good.

220
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:41,195
Careful, everyone.

221
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:45,241
Go.

222
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:46,200
Run.

223
00:13:46,283 --> 00:13:48,619
Faster. Come on.

224
00:13:48,702 --> 00:13:50,663
Faster. Those guys are ahead of us.

225
00:13:50,746 --> 00:13:51,580
Careful.

226
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:54,041
Careful, we don't know
how deep the water is.

227
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:55,543
The stairs are steep.

228
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:58,712
James, hurry. Those guys are ahead of us!

229
00:13:58,796 --> 00:14:00,005
Run, James, run!

230
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:01,298
Run, Sun, run!

231
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:03,717
We're behind.
Hurry, go for the crates first!

232
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:06,971
Get me a crate first!

233
00:14:07,054 --> 00:14:09,056
Dong-hyun, we need a crate first!

234
00:14:09,139 --> 00:14:10,140
I got the crate.

235
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:12,351
One, two, three. Okay.

236
00:14:12,434 --> 00:14:13,769
Quick.

237
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:17,439
You're doing great, guys! Good pace!

238
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:21,485
The crate actually wasn't that heavy
because we carried it together.

239
00:14:22,111 --> 00:14:23,487
One, two. All right.

240
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:24,530
This is good.

241
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:25,823
Great job, guys.

242
00:14:25,906 --> 00:14:26,949
One, two.

243
00:14:27,032 --> 00:14:29,618
-Great speed.
-One, two.

244
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:30,786
-Nice work, guys.
-All right.

245
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:32,663
You go, Amotti. I'll help her.

246
00:14:33,664 --> 00:14:34,832
Come on, hurry.

247
00:14:35,457 --> 00:14:36,917
Come on, hurry.

248
00:14:38,669 --> 00:14:40,004
Oh my goodness!

249
00:14:40,087 --> 00:14:42,798
We needed to fetch a crate
as quickly as possible.

250
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:46,010
Yeah, that's it! Come on!

251
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:48,804
Somebody help James out!

252
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:52,266
Here, James. Let's go.

253
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:53,684
Come on, hurry.

254
00:14:54,768 --> 00:14:55,728
Don't rush.

255
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:57,229
There we go.

256
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:05,070
I'd never been on a zip line before,

257
00:15:05,154 --> 00:15:07,239
so it was a bit nerve-racking,

258
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:09,909
but I told myself I'd be fine
as long as I kept calm and steady.

259
00:15:16,206 --> 00:15:17,917
Come on, bring more.

260
00:15:19,251 --> 00:15:22,212
I didn't find it particularly heavy
when I first picked it up.

261
00:15:22,796 --> 00:15:24,840
It wasn't challenging
to transport it to the other side.

262
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,010
I think we can win this.

263
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:35,893
The first one I picked up
was three bags tied together.

264
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:37,102
It wasn't easy

265
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:39,772
moving quickly with it
because the ramp was so steep,

266
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:41,565
but it wasn't
particularly difficult either.

267
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:43,400
Careful.

268
00:15:47,279 --> 00:15:49,490
The plan was for me
to stay off the ladder.

269
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:51,575
We decided there was no point
in me even attempting it.

270
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:55,204
In the time I made one round trip,
the bags would pile up anyway.

271
00:15:55,287 --> 00:15:57,373
So I would just load up the cart,

272
00:15:57,456 --> 00:16:00,167
and then Sung-bin would come down

273
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:01,877
and push it up with me.

274
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:03,671
That one's heavy.

275
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:04,964
I don't know why they're tied together.

276
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:09,051
Everyone's been back at least once, right?

277
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:09,969
Yes.

278
00:16:10,052 --> 00:16:11,345
Let's give it a go with these.

279
00:16:11,428 --> 00:16:12,304
One, two.

280
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:19,103
One, two.

281
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:21,772
It was easier than expected.

282
00:16:21,855 --> 00:16:24,900
I think each load
was around six or seven bags.

283
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:28,570
Pushing it together
definitely made it quite manageable.

284
00:16:29,321 --> 00:16:32,449
7 BAGS

285
00:16:34,201 --> 00:16:36,495
The first time I carried a crate,

286
00:16:36,578 --> 00:16:40,124
it was with someone else,
so it didn't feel that heavy.

287
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:43,544
But it wasn't efficient to have
two people carrying a crate each time,

288
00:16:43,627 --> 00:16:45,129
and I realized it wouldn't cut it.

289
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:50,092
So I decided to carry one by myself.

290
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:53,470
There was no real way to make it easier,

291
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:55,556
so I took it on my back.

292
00:16:58,142 --> 00:17:02,396
The crates were very heavy,
but James did an amazing job.

293
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:06,275
I was in awe
that he could carry the crate alone.

294
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,069
How does James lift this up?

295
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,179
I need a crate!

296
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:36,847
A crate? Got it.

297
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,475
Dong-hyun, she needs a crate.

298
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:40,476
-What?
-A crate.

299
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:41,518
-A crate?
-Yeah.

300
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:52,696
Team Thailand brought over a lot of crates
early on in the match.

301
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,782
But my team wasn't bringing me many.

302
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:56,116
I kept running out of crates

303
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:58,285
and realized we needed to
focus on them early on.

304
00:17:58,368 --> 00:18:00,329
Team Thailand is on their fourth crate,

305
00:18:00,412 --> 00:18:01,497
while we're only on our second.

306
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:05,918
Can you guys get me another one?

307
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:13,926
That was our plan from the beginning.

308
00:18:15,135 --> 00:18:19,515
James and Sun would bring up
around four crates at the start.

309
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:26,897
So I'd be able to work through them
quickly without any downtime.

310
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:37,157
I don't have any crates.

311
00:18:37,741 --> 00:18:38,909
She needs crates.

312
00:18:39,993 --> 00:18:41,703
We definitely have an advantage
on the zip line.

313
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:47,918
Superbon is definitely
much faster than her.

314
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:50,003
I mean, he's fast when he's boxing,
after all.

315
00:18:50,087 --> 00:18:52,381
I have too much idle time right now.

316
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:54,800
This really works in our favor.

317
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:05,769
5TH CRATE, 4TH CRATE

318
00:19:09,314 --> 00:19:11,525
More crates! We need more crates!

319
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:13,235
More crates!

320
00:19:13,777 --> 00:19:17,614
Superbon was super fast on the zip line.

321
00:19:18,615 --> 00:19:20,951
It really motivated me.

322
00:19:21,034 --> 00:19:22,369
My confidence grew,

323
00:19:23,078 --> 00:19:25,372
and I went into beast mode.

324
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:27,583
That's when it happened.

325
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:34,840
I thought, "What's that sound?"

326
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:42,014
I was urging myself on saying,
"Come on! Don't give up!"

327
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:46,602
It was like a beat to keep me in step.

328
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:50,439
You know, like soldiers.

329
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,233
Okay!

330
00:20:00,449 --> 00:20:04,411
Bellowing has the effect
of encouraging our team

331
00:20:04,494 --> 00:20:07,664
and intimidating the opponent.

332
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:08,832
Great job, James!

333
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:10,542
You're doing amazing!

334
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:20,093
That got to us. It was a thunderous sound.

335
00:20:20,177 --> 00:20:22,137
It actually did
knock our confidence a bit.

336
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:25,599
That James guy
turned out to be a dark horse.

337
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:30,395
This is heavy.

338
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:31,313
Here.

339
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:33,023
Help me carry this.

340
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:33,941
One, two, three.

341
00:20:34,024 --> 00:20:35,525
Dong-hyun, get me a crate!

342
00:20:35,609 --> 00:20:37,110
Dong-hyun, get me a crate!

343
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:39,696
Seung-yeon, you keep going.
We need to get crates.

344
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:43,867
After moving a few crates,
I thought we could leave them for a bit.

345
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:46,370
But Eun-sil transported them
faster than expected.

346
00:20:46,453 --> 00:20:48,288
I understood
that she didn't have any crates,

347
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:50,249
but my hands
were already full of sandbags.

348
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:51,500
I don't have any crates.

349
00:20:52,417 --> 00:20:53,252
I'll go.

350
00:20:56,296 --> 00:20:59,883
Idle time on the zip line meant

351
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:03,512
that we weren't collecting
as many goods as we could.

352
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:04,429
I'm off.

353
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:08,141
So we really had to keep moving nonstop.

354
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:16,358
-One, two, three.
-One, two.

355
00:21:17,859 --> 00:21:19,695
That's when things started to look up.

356
00:21:20,737 --> 00:21:22,864
Having a teammate
jumping in to help like that

357
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:24,074
was incredibly motivating.

358
00:21:24,157 --> 00:21:26,368
-All right.
-All right. One, two, three!

359
00:21:27,452 --> 00:21:29,955
Sung-bin went to help out the other guys,

360
00:21:30,038 --> 00:21:31,665
so I tried pushing it alone.

361
00:21:39,756 --> 00:21:42,634
8 BAGS

362
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:45,804
Damn, that's slippery.

363
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,347
Damn, that's slippery.

364
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,933
I tried to go up the ramp,

365
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:52,436
but I skidded backward
before I could reach the first cleat.

366
00:21:58,525 --> 00:22:00,902
All I needed was just one more step,

367
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:03,155
but I kept skidding backward.

368
00:22:03,238 --> 00:22:04,823
It was driving me nuts.

369
00:22:05,699 --> 00:22:06,783
Man, this is too slippery.

370
00:22:08,785 --> 00:22:11,538
Dong-hyun, Min-jae's struggling
to push the cart up alone.

371
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:13,165
-Huh?
-He can't manage.

372
00:22:13,248 --> 00:22:14,166
Sung-bin, you've got to go.

373
00:22:16,918 --> 00:22:19,421
I mean, it was my one job
to push the cart.

374
00:22:19,921 --> 00:22:24,760
So not being able to do that
was humiliating and frustrating.

375
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:26,678
It really put me off my game.

376
00:22:32,851 --> 00:22:33,852
Should we take the sandbags up?

377
00:22:34,394 --> 00:22:36,021
Okay, I'll go load them up.

378
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:43,862
-Let's give this a go.
-Let's go.

379
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:47,657
One, two.

380
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:53,872
9 BAGS

381
00:22:56,416 --> 00:22:57,542
It's too heavy.

382
00:22:58,126 --> 00:22:59,002
It's too heavy.

383
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:00,545
Try one cleat at a time.

384
00:23:00,629 --> 00:23:01,755
I can't reach it in one step.

385
00:23:03,423 --> 00:23:05,133
When I was pushing the cart up,

386
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:08,553
I realized that my legs were too short.

387
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:13,809
I couldn't step far enough
to reach the cleat in a single step.

388
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:15,769
One, two!

389
00:23:23,068 --> 00:23:26,238
I was pushing against the cleat
with my feet.

390
00:23:26,321 --> 00:23:27,906
Instead of just pulling with my arms,

391
00:23:27,989 --> 00:23:31,451
I had to push with my feet
and pull with my arms at the same time.

392
00:23:31,535 --> 00:23:32,953
One, two!

393
00:23:33,036 --> 00:23:34,454
I'm pulling. Push!

394
00:23:36,164 --> 00:23:38,834
I think the load was just too heavy,

395
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:41,294
but I had to push it up
by any means possible.

396
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:42,546
One, two.

397
00:23:45,757 --> 00:23:46,591
Push!

398
00:23:47,425 --> 00:23:48,844
-One, two.
-Push!

399
00:23:49,553 --> 00:23:50,387
Good.

400
00:23:50,887 --> 00:23:54,850
It was really tough,
but I couldn't give up.

401
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:57,227
-One, two.
-Push!

402
00:23:57,310 --> 00:23:58,228
Almost there.

403
00:23:58,311 --> 00:23:59,354
We're almost there. Come on!

404
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:14,744
Team Thailand is struggling!

405
00:24:15,537 --> 00:24:17,789
I get encouraged
when I see my opponents struggling,

406
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:19,916
because it makes me realize
I'm not the only one.

407
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:22,919
If they're having a tough time of it,
I need to go harder.

408
00:24:23,003 --> 00:24:25,213
I can't slack off.

409
00:24:25,714 --> 00:24:29,050
That's how I fueled myself to keep going.

410
00:24:32,429 --> 00:24:33,763
Way to go, Seung-yeon!

411
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:35,098
Run one more step and we win!

412
00:24:35,599 --> 00:24:36,892
Walk one more step and we win!

413
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:39,936
There was so much sand in my shoes

414
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:43,106
that it felt like I had sandbags
attached to my feet.

415
00:24:44,232 --> 00:24:46,943
Going uphill got harder and harder.

416
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:48,987
My legs got heavier and heavier.

417
00:24:50,238 --> 00:24:52,949
The intensity of the weight
was slowly wearing me down.

418
00:24:53,867 --> 00:24:56,912
But I knew I couldn't rest,
so I gritted my teeth and kept going.

419
00:24:56,995 --> 00:24:57,996
Just need to keep at it.

420
00:24:58,079 --> 00:25:00,040
-Yeah, just keep at it.
-That's the spirit, Amotti.

421
00:25:00,123 --> 00:25:01,166
We just keep going!

422
00:25:01,249 --> 00:25:02,417
-That's it!
-One, two, three!

423
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:04,920
-All right!
-Let's do this!

424
00:25:05,003 --> 00:25:06,129
Let's go!

425
00:25:06,213 --> 00:25:07,214
Let's go!

426
00:25:09,299 --> 00:25:10,342
You're doing great, Sung-bin.

427
00:25:10,842 --> 00:25:12,260
Republic of Korea!

428
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:13,595
Let's bring it!

429
00:25:13,678 --> 00:25:14,888
Let's bring it!

430
00:25:16,765 --> 00:25:18,099
Five minutes to go!

431
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:19,476
Five minutes to go!

432
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:21,853
Five minutes!

433
00:25:22,395 --> 00:25:24,231
Come on, Min-jae! We're almost there!

434
00:25:24,731 --> 00:25:26,733
-Just five more minutes!
-We're almost there, guys!

435
00:25:28,276 --> 00:25:31,529
Hearing my teammates
cheering each other on kept me going.

436
00:25:33,114 --> 00:25:34,616
It gave me a power boost.

437
00:25:36,117 --> 00:25:37,577
6 BAGS

438
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:42,582
Min-jae.

439
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:44,125
You're almost there, Min-jae!

440
00:25:44,876 --> 00:25:45,877
You're almost there, Min-jae!

441
00:25:46,461 --> 00:25:48,546
Straighten your arms! That's it!

442
00:25:48,630 --> 00:25:49,464
Come on!

443
00:25:49,547 --> 00:25:51,466
All right! Way to go.

444
00:25:51,549 --> 00:25:52,550
Come on!

445
00:25:52,634 --> 00:25:54,844
That's it! Five more steps! Go, Min-jae!

446
00:25:57,889 --> 00:25:59,975
When I heard them urging me on,
I couldn't stop.

447
00:26:00,058 --> 00:26:01,393
It powered me on.

448
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:05,313
Come on, you're almost there!

449
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:13,321
Min-jae totally nailed his role.

450
00:26:13,405 --> 00:26:15,031
He couldn't possibly have done any more.

451
00:26:17,617 --> 00:26:18,910
Suddenly, I had a nosebleed.

452
00:26:18,994 --> 00:26:20,912
I guess it really did take it out of me.

453
00:26:20,996 --> 00:26:21,997
KIM MIN-JAE
SSIREUM WRESTLER

454
00:26:25,959 --> 00:26:27,711
It was backbreaking work.

455
00:26:29,629 --> 00:26:32,757
You can tell from the fact
that we're slowing down and pausing

456
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:33,925
that we're losing steam.

457
00:26:34,009 --> 00:26:35,719
It's getting harder and harder.

458
00:26:39,222 --> 00:26:40,390
Go, James.

459
00:26:46,313 --> 00:26:47,522
Yes!

460
00:26:47,605 --> 00:26:50,233
They've lost their mojo. They're folding.

461
00:26:54,112 --> 00:26:57,115
If Superbon has no crates to transport,

462
00:26:57,198 --> 00:27:00,201
he can only sit idle and waste time.

463
00:27:00,285 --> 00:27:01,453
Ploy, help me with this.

464
00:27:01,953 --> 00:27:03,330
Ploy, lift this.

465
00:27:03,955 --> 00:27:05,165
Onto your back, right?

466
00:27:05,749 --> 00:27:09,210
I need to sacrifice myself for Superbon,

467
00:27:10,754 --> 00:27:14,507
who's working hard on the zip line.

468
00:27:15,550 --> 00:27:17,969
I need to ensure
his efforts don't go to waste.

469
00:27:18,928 --> 00:27:20,263
You're a star, James.

470
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:26,269
Watching James carry the crate
on his back by himself

471
00:27:26,353 --> 00:27:29,064
made me feel bad
about not doing my fair share.

472
00:27:29,647 --> 00:27:33,443
I felt I ought to be working too.

473
00:27:34,277 --> 00:27:37,322
After all, this fight wasn't for me alone,

474
00:27:37,405 --> 00:27:38,823
but for the team.

475
00:27:38,907 --> 00:27:42,410
It was a fight for Team Thailand.

476
00:27:44,662 --> 00:27:47,040
Three minutes left!

477
00:27:47,665 --> 00:27:48,625
Three minutes to go!

478
00:27:49,542 --> 00:27:50,794
Come on, let's go get a crate.

479
00:27:51,795 --> 00:27:53,004
Get me one more crate.

480
00:28:01,763 --> 00:28:04,265
Those guys only have four crates left.

481
00:28:04,766 --> 00:28:05,809
Let's get the crates.

482
00:28:05,892 --> 00:28:07,852
-Just the crates!
-Yeah, just the crates!

483
00:28:07,936 --> 00:28:08,812
Every crate helps!

484
00:28:09,396 --> 00:28:11,272
Come on, Republic of Korea!
Keep going till the end!

485
00:28:11,356 --> 00:28:13,817
-Way to go, guys!
-One, two, three.

486
00:28:16,986 --> 00:28:19,072
One, two. Good.

487
00:28:19,155 --> 00:28:20,073
One, two.

488
00:28:20,907 --> 00:28:22,742
Anucha, push!

489
00:28:22,826 --> 00:28:24,828
Come on!

490
00:28:24,911 --> 00:28:26,329
We're almost out of time.

491
00:28:26,413 --> 00:28:28,331
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three!

492
00:28:28,998 --> 00:28:30,583
-Make sure you get this in.
-Don't worry, I got it.

493
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:42,846
-It's not over yet!
-No.

494
00:28:43,388 --> 00:28:45,223
James, take the other side. Come on.

495
00:28:49,269 --> 00:28:50,520
A minute and a half left.

496
00:28:53,773 --> 00:28:55,233
Hey, just give me one.

497
00:28:55,316 --> 00:28:57,152
Here. Here's a single.

498
00:28:57,777 --> 00:28:58,611
Give me one more.

499
00:28:58,695 --> 00:29:01,239
-Hurry! Only a minute to go!
-One minute!

500
00:29:02,615 --> 00:29:03,658
One minute.

501
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:05,201
We won't make it. Let's just go.

502
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:06,619
A minute's all we have anyway.

503
00:29:06,703 --> 00:29:07,537
Let's go.

504
00:29:07,620 --> 00:29:09,831
I think we're better off
helping push the cart up.

505
00:29:12,375 --> 00:29:14,627
With a minute to go, I was torn.

506
00:29:14,711 --> 00:29:17,255
This 40 kg load
could be the deciding factor.

507
00:29:17,338 --> 00:29:19,007
Forty-seven seconds! Just one more trip.

508
00:29:19,090 --> 00:29:21,217
Just one more. No!

509
00:29:22,886 --> 00:29:24,512
One, two, push!

510
00:29:31,686 --> 00:29:33,438
We can't stop. We've got to keep going.

511
00:29:38,526 --> 00:29:39,360
Thirty seconds!

512
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:41,029
Everyone, help get them all down!

513
00:29:44,866 --> 00:29:45,784
Let's do one more load.

514
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:47,035
All right, let's do it.

515
00:29:48,077 --> 00:29:49,954
Thirty seconds. We have to go now.

516
00:29:50,038 --> 00:29:51,581
Thirty seconds. Come on, start pushing!

517
00:29:51,664 --> 00:29:53,333
-No, wait.
-Just go.

518
00:29:55,126 --> 00:29:56,002
One, two, three!

519
00:29:56,085 --> 00:29:57,670
Out of the way.

520
00:30:00,548 --> 00:30:02,759
We kept going until the very last second

521
00:30:02,842 --> 00:30:05,929
to move as much stuff as we could.

522
00:30:06,930 --> 00:30:10,016
We need to add this last crate.

523
00:30:10,850 --> 00:30:13,228
This is what's going to get us the win.

524
00:30:15,104 --> 00:30:16,022
You need to get them in now!

525
00:30:16,648 --> 00:30:18,066
-Min-jae, drop them down!
-Okay.

526
00:30:19,484 --> 00:30:21,194
-Ten seconds!
-Ten seconds.

527
00:30:21,277 --> 00:30:22,278
Ten seconds.

528
00:30:24,447 --> 00:30:25,532
Five seconds!

529
00:30:25,615 --> 00:30:27,826
We need to get this crate in on time.

530
00:30:27,909 --> 00:30:29,619
This is what's going to clinch the win.

531
00:30:32,914 --> 00:30:33,998
The time! One second!

532
00:30:34,082 --> 00:30:35,208
Come on!

533
00:30:43,633 --> 00:30:44,551
Stop.

534
00:30:45,134 --> 00:30:46,302
Game over.

535
00:30:53,309 --> 00:30:56,688
After the match, we were all
just trying to catch our breath.

536
00:30:56,771 --> 00:31:03,069
It was evidence that we'd all been
operating at max capacity.

537
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:05,530
I'm so proud of you.

538
00:31:08,658 --> 00:31:09,701
I feel great!

539
00:31:12,912 --> 00:31:15,790
Man, whoever created
these quests for Physical: Asia

540
00:31:15,874 --> 00:31:20,879
really knows how to push you
to your absolute limit.

541
00:31:21,754 --> 00:31:24,382
It was really tough. Insanely tough.

542
00:31:24,465 --> 00:31:28,177
The final load of around 40 kg
that we didn't manage to get in on time

543
00:31:28,761 --> 00:31:30,388
continued to play on my mind.

544
00:31:32,849 --> 00:31:36,561
The second quest of Physical: Asia.

545
00:31:37,228 --> 00:31:39,022
Shipwreck transportation match.

546
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:43,359
Here are the results
of the Republic of Korea versus Thailand.

547
00:31:54,370 --> 00:31:55,622
It's full to the brim.

548
00:31:55,705 --> 00:31:56,915
Looking good. It's packed.

549
00:31:57,540 --> 00:31:58,666
The crates are on top.

550
00:32:00,001 --> 00:32:00,960
The Republic of Korea.

551
00:32:03,046 --> 00:32:04,380
Our reputation hinges on this.

552
00:32:04,464 --> 00:32:06,716
We need to show everyone
how formidable we are.

553
00:32:12,388 --> 00:32:13,473
That's a lot.

554
00:32:14,557 --> 00:32:16,309
2,120 kg.

555
00:32:16,976 --> 00:32:18,186
We did amazing.

556
00:32:18,770 --> 00:32:23,358
Out of a total of 6 tons,
we brought back 2,100 kg.

557
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:25,443
That surely had to be a winning score.

558
00:32:25,526 --> 00:32:29,155
It was proof that we'd worked hard
and given it our all.

559
00:32:31,491 --> 00:32:33,368
That really is a lot.

560
00:32:33,451 --> 00:32:35,119
Keep your eyes on the scoreboard.

561
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:36,120
Thailand.

562
00:32:36,829 --> 00:32:38,039
I can't watch this.

563
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:44,754
The last digit is the same.

564
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:46,839
Come on.

565
00:32:47,632 --> 00:32:50,009
Two. Give us a two.

566
00:32:51,177 --> 00:32:52,178
Two.

567
00:32:52,762 --> 00:32:53,805
I can't tell.

568
00:32:53,888 --> 00:32:54,764
One thousand.

569
00:32:54,847 --> 00:32:58,559
Everyone did their best,
and we had nothing left in the tank.

570
00:32:58,643 --> 00:33:01,104
I'm sure we've won.

571
00:33:01,187 --> 00:33:02,230
Come on.

572
00:33:02,313 --> 00:33:03,773
Two. It has to start with a two.

573
00:33:03,856 --> 00:33:06,526
One. Come on, please.

574
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:12,907
1,380 kg.

575
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:20,206
Republic of Korea!

576
00:33:20,289 --> 00:33:21,624
-We did it!
-We did it!

577
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:27,964
That's not even close.

578
00:33:28,047 --> 00:33:29,841
-It's the sandbags.
-The sandbags.

579
00:33:31,926 --> 00:33:35,054
THAILAND
16 CRATES, 29 BAGS

580
00:33:37,849 --> 00:33:40,560
REPUBLIC OF KOREA
16 CRATES, 66 BAGS

581
00:33:40,643 --> 00:33:42,061
They got way more bags.
We can't argue with that.

582
00:33:43,229 --> 00:33:44,188
I chose the wrong strategy.

583
00:33:44,272 --> 00:33:45,982
I thought crates would be
the deciding factor

584
00:33:46,065 --> 00:33:48,568
and placed too much focus on them.

585
00:33:50,445 --> 00:33:52,530
Bring more crates!

586
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:54,699
Bring as many crates as you can!

587
00:33:55,783 --> 00:33:58,536
I think Team Korea had a good strategy

588
00:33:58,619 --> 00:34:00,163
and deployed their people well.

589
00:34:00,246 --> 00:34:02,040
They had a good system going.

590
00:34:03,082 --> 00:34:04,083
I'll do it.

591
00:34:04,167 --> 00:34:06,794
Everyone knew what they were
meant to be doing and when.

592
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:09,172
I'm out of crates! Get me crates!

593
00:34:09,255 --> 00:34:10,089
She needs crates.

594
00:34:10,173 --> 00:34:12,341
I think that's why
they were more efficient.

595
00:34:12,425 --> 00:34:14,135
They didn't take any breaks either.

596
00:34:14,218 --> 00:34:15,053
Ten minutes.

597
00:34:15,636 --> 00:34:16,846
Revealing the interim weight score.

598
00:34:17,388 --> 00:34:20,266
-Yes! We're leading by a huge margin!
-We need to keep going!

599
00:34:20,808 --> 00:34:21,893
Keep at it!

600
00:34:22,393 --> 00:34:23,227
Nice!

601
00:34:23,811 --> 00:34:25,271
-Let's go.
-Being in the lead feels good!

602
00:34:25,354 --> 00:34:27,732
Each and every one of us
fulfilled our roles perfectly.

603
00:34:27,815 --> 00:34:29,901
Our teamwork was close to perfection.

604
00:34:30,401 --> 00:34:31,402
Bravo.

605
00:34:33,029 --> 00:34:34,363
The winning team is

606
00:34:35,114 --> 00:34:36,324
Team Republic of Korea.

607
00:34:38,534 --> 00:34:39,911
Great work, everyone.

608
00:34:41,579 --> 00:34:44,207
The losing team is Team Thailand.

609
00:34:44,290 --> 00:34:47,126
I wish we could continue
in the competition

610
00:34:47,210 --> 00:34:48,669
and redeem ourselves.

611
00:34:59,931 --> 00:35:02,850
What do you guys think of Team Türkiye?

612
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:06,270
I think we can handle them.

613
00:35:06,354 --> 00:35:10,691
They're exhausted from
all the matches they played yesterday,

614
00:35:10,775 --> 00:35:12,151
but we only played two.

615
00:35:12,235 --> 00:35:13,402
And I bet

616
00:35:13,486 --> 00:35:16,614
-they're thrown off by the fact
-Isai?

617
00:35:16,697 --> 00:35:19,951
-that we have a new team member, Isai.
-Let's go, Isai.

618
00:35:20,535 --> 00:35:21,661
INDONESIA

619
00:35:21,744 --> 00:35:25,414
DUE TO MARCUS GIDEON'S INJURY,
ISAI KESEK HAS TAKEN HIS PLACE

620
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:31,546
ISAI KESEK
BODYBUILDER

621
00:35:32,213 --> 00:35:34,257
How are you feeling, Isai?
Are you ready for this?

622
00:35:35,424 --> 00:35:37,176
Yeah, 100%.

623
00:35:57,029 --> 00:35:58,114
Guys.

624
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:03,786
Yo, you ready for today?

625
00:36:04,370 --> 00:36:05,204
-Ready.
-Of course.

626
00:36:05,288 --> 00:36:07,456
-You sure?
-Of course. Bring it on.

627
00:36:07,540 --> 00:36:08,958
You wanna think about it again?

628
00:36:09,542 --> 00:36:10,376
No?

629
00:36:10,459 --> 00:36:11,586
Maybe you, yeah?

630
00:36:12,420 --> 00:36:13,462
Maybe you should.

631
00:36:15,339 --> 00:36:16,340
We've thought enough.

632
00:36:21,971 --> 00:36:23,389
I was trying to provoke them.

633
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:24,849
ANIL BERK BAKI
NATIONAL TEAM SAILOR

634
00:36:24,932 --> 00:36:26,058
To get them motivated, you know?

635
00:36:26,142 --> 00:36:29,729
So I threw out a couple of jibes,
but they didn't react to them at all.

636
00:36:29,812 --> 00:36:31,981
It kinda irked me, to be honest.

637
00:36:32,565 --> 00:36:34,525
Ask them if they've
booked their plane tickets.

638
00:36:34,609 --> 00:36:37,528
My friend's asking you,
did you check your tickets?

639
00:36:37,612 --> 00:36:38,529
Airplane tickets.

640
00:36:38,613 --> 00:36:40,114
The writing's on the wall for them.

641
00:36:40,615 --> 00:36:42,617
Today is their last day of filming.

642
00:36:43,701 --> 00:36:46,120
Yeah, I hope you can keep that spirit.

643
00:36:46,204 --> 00:36:47,038
Yeah.

644
00:36:49,081 --> 00:36:52,710
In that moment, I felt like I was on fire.

645
00:36:52,793 --> 00:36:55,129
I was fuming inside.

646
00:36:55,630 --> 00:36:56,797
I couldn't wait…

647
00:36:56,881 --> 00:36:57,882
JEREMIAH LAKHWANI
HYBRID ATHLETE

648
00:36:57,965 --> 00:36:59,217
…to start the second quest

649
00:36:59,300 --> 00:37:02,637
and prove to them
we weren't just rolling over for them.

650
00:37:03,262 --> 00:37:09,227
They were also giving us the side-eye
when they picked us.

651
00:37:09,310 --> 00:37:12,313
We know full well
what those looks and smirks mean.

652
00:37:14,023 --> 00:37:16,525
Today's our chance

653
00:37:16,609 --> 00:37:20,321
to wipe those smirks off their faces.

654
00:37:24,533 --> 00:37:28,120
The second quest of Physical: Asia.

655
00:37:28,204 --> 00:37:29,497
The game between Türkiye…

656
00:37:32,333 --> 00:37:35,628
and Indonesia will now begin.

657
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:38,005
Ready…

658
00:37:48,516 --> 00:37:49,475
These steps are steep.

659
00:37:50,726 --> 00:37:52,019
Watch the steps.

660
00:37:52,103 --> 00:37:53,604
Try not to step in the water.

661
00:37:58,901 --> 00:38:03,155
First, we went straight for the bags
and sorted them out

662
00:38:03,739 --> 00:38:06,993
while Isai dealt with the crates.

663
00:38:09,036 --> 00:38:11,080
Come on, team! Let's do this!

664
00:38:13,332 --> 00:38:16,127
Nice, Isai! Good, Isai!

665
00:38:16,752 --> 00:38:17,670
Come on!

666
00:38:18,838 --> 00:38:22,675
As soon as the game started,
my teammates were like deer in headlights.

667
00:38:22,758 --> 00:38:24,385
They had no idea what to do.

668
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:27,263
It's right there. Take it.

669
00:38:27,346 --> 00:38:29,223
Don't take this. Take that.

670
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:31,100
Can't you see the bags, man?

671
00:38:31,726 --> 00:38:33,019
These are three tied together.

672
00:38:33,602 --> 00:38:34,603
Am I meant to take them like this?

673
00:38:35,187 --> 00:38:37,898
-I can't take them apart!
-It doesn't matter, just take them.

674
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:42,069
We didn't realize some of them
were tied together in threes

675
00:38:42,153 --> 00:38:44,530
and ended up wasting a bit of time
figuring things out.

676
00:38:45,823 --> 00:38:48,659
Isai, give it to me. Take your time.

677
00:38:50,786 --> 00:38:51,620
Let's go.

678
00:38:51,704 --> 00:38:53,998
Put it up here, Igedz.

679
00:38:54,081 --> 00:38:55,499
Come on.

680
00:38:56,751 --> 00:38:58,669
I was getting annoyed at that point.

681
00:38:59,295 --> 00:39:01,005
Our teamwork really wasn't great.

682
00:39:09,930 --> 00:39:12,933
At first, 50 kg seemed far too heavy.

683
00:39:13,517 --> 00:39:16,645
It was difficult to push and handle.

684
00:39:21,817 --> 00:39:23,819
We were lagging behind,
but it didn't matter

685
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:27,114
because we had a great strategy
and sound tactics.

686
00:39:27,198 --> 00:39:28,240
Come on, Anıl.

687
00:39:28,324 --> 00:39:30,117
-One, two.
-One, two.

688
00:39:30,201 --> 00:39:31,410
Don't drop it!

689
00:39:34,789 --> 00:39:35,956
Don't drop it!

690
00:39:40,294 --> 00:39:43,172
I couldn't believe it.
It left me speechless.

691
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:48,219
We're carrying bags on top of the crates

692
00:39:48,302 --> 00:39:50,471
early on in the game
while we still have the energy.

693
00:40:18,582 --> 00:40:20,918
One, two, three.

694
00:40:22,545 --> 00:40:25,714
Recep, hold the bags down
with your other hand.

695
00:40:30,719 --> 00:40:33,139
Maria, don't do this. No one can carry it.

696
00:40:33,722 --> 00:40:35,099
Separate them out into singles.

697
00:40:35,182 --> 00:40:36,892
That's 60 kg. None of us can carry it.

698
00:40:38,686 --> 00:40:40,855
-Ali, put one on my shoulder.
-One?

699
00:40:40,938 --> 00:40:42,314
No, the bundle of three.

700
00:40:42,398 --> 00:40:43,732
-Come on.
-Let's go.

701
00:40:44,483 --> 00:40:45,943
-Are you sure?
-Positive!

702
00:40:52,741 --> 00:40:56,078
I obviously had to show them
how strong Turkish women are,

703
00:40:56,162 --> 00:41:00,458
so I carried the sandbags
over my shoulder.

704
00:41:06,046 --> 00:41:07,756
Ogeday, that's more efficient.

705
00:41:08,591 --> 00:41:09,467
It's much easier.

706
00:41:31,238 --> 00:41:34,283
I forgot to hook the tether
and had to go back three times.

707
00:41:38,245 --> 00:41:39,747
I dropped my glove.

708
00:41:45,586 --> 00:41:46,754
Not again!

709
00:41:49,173 --> 00:41:52,259
It was because
the Indonesian girl next to me

710
00:41:52,343 --> 00:41:54,011
was going back and forth so fast.

711
00:41:54,094 --> 00:41:56,472
She was moving like the wind.

712
00:42:16,784 --> 00:42:20,204
She was shouting and hooting
like she was Tarzan or something.

713
00:42:22,456 --> 00:42:23,666
Let's go!

714
00:42:25,292 --> 00:42:28,420
My teammates are bringing
the crates up onto the deck,

715
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:31,715
and I don't want to keep them waiting.

716
00:42:31,799 --> 00:42:36,512
So I need to keep moving
until all the crates are transported.

717
00:42:41,267 --> 00:42:42,518
Hey, I'll help load them up.

718
00:42:46,105 --> 00:42:50,526
As the team leader,
I want to lead my team to victory

719
00:42:50,609 --> 00:42:54,530
and prove that
we're more than capable of winning.

720
00:43:00,452 --> 00:43:05,416
8 BAGS

721
00:43:06,458 --> 00:43:07,626
-It's heavy.
-Let's push harder.

722
00:43:08,669 --> 00:43:10,087
You try pulling from the front.

723
00:43:10,170 --> 00:43:11,005
Hold the cart there.

724
00:43:12,881 --> 00:43:15,134
-Should we add five more?
-No.

725
00:43:15,217 --> 00:43:16,093
We can do it.

726
00:43:18,470 --> 00:43:20,222
-We need more sandbags!
-Maria!

727
00:43:21,181 --> 00:43:25,936
10 BAGS

728
00:43:28,981 --> 00:43:30,024
Pull!

729
00:43:58,427 --> 00:43:59,470
Let's go!

730
00:44:02,264 --> 00:44:04,892
Come on, Igedz.
We've got to win this, man.

731
00:44:04,975 --> 00:44:05,976
We've got to win this.

732
00:44:06,685 --> 00:44:10,272
That was the moment I was convinced
that if we worked together,

733
00:44:10,356 --> 00:44:12,232
we could beat Team Türkiye.

734
00:44:18,614 --> 00:44:20,532
They're adding in their sandbags.

735
00:44:20,616 --> 00:44:22,701
-What?
-They're adding in their sandbags.

736
00:44:23,911 --> 00:44:26,455
It was one of our tactics

737
00:44:26,538 --> 00:44:30,459
to let the bags accumulate
and take a huge load in the cart in one go

738
00:44:30,542 --> 00:44:32,086
rather than do many trips with it.

739
00:44:32,753 --> 00:44:33,587
15 MINUTES AGO

740
00:44:33,671 --> 00:44:35,673
We can collect the bags without the cart,

741
00:44:35,756 --> 00:44:38,050
so let's leave it until the end
to add them in.

742
00:44:38,884 --> 00:44:42,429
But while we were
busting our guts collecting bags,

743
00:44:42,930 --> 00:44:45,849
they were already up there
unloading theirs into the hold.

744
00:44:46,517 --> 00:44:49,144
That was our wake-up call.

745
00:44:54,066 --> 00:44:55,109
I'll go down.

746
00:45:11,417 --> 00:45:12,251
Come down!

747
00:45:13,877 --> 00:45:15,838
-No, just one of you will do.
-Move.

748
00:45:16,672 --> 00:45:17,840
One, two.

749
00:45:17,923 --> 00:45:18,882
14 BAGS

750
00:45:18,966 --> 00:45:19,842
Is it moving?

751
00:45:24,805 --> 00:45:26,348
Use the posts for support.

752
00:45:26,432 --> 00:45:28,183
There are posts on the side, Ogeday.

753
00:45:32,104 --> 00:45:36,650
Honestly, I didn't realize
the ramp was that steep.

754
00:45:37,234 --> 00:45:41,280
I was totally out of breath.
It was extremely backbreaking.

755
00:45:43,031 --> 00:45:43,866
We're here.

756
00:45:44,366 --> 00:45:45,742
Hang in there. This is nothing.

757
00:45:49,246 --> 00:45:50,122
You guys go.

758
00:45:50,664 --> 00:45:52,291
Get back there.

759
00:45:55,961 --> 00:45:57,004
Ten minutes.

760
00:45:57,087 --> 00:45:58,547
Ten minutes left.

761
00:45:59,715 --> 00:46:01,049
Revealing the interim weight score.

762
00:46:10,017 --> 00:46:11,643
I was in utter shock.

763
00:46:16,273 --> 00:46:19,651
It was devastating.

764
00:46:21,403 --> 00:46:23,322
Those guys have taken up
a boatload of bags.

765
00:46:25,574 --> 00:46:27,201
What if we lose?

766
00:46:27,284 --> 00:46:30,954
And what if it's my fault?

767
00:46:33,290 --> 00:46:38,003
When I saw the score,
I tried not to get too excited.

768
00:46:42,174 --> 00:46:45,552
I did think we had it in the bag.

769
00:46:47,137 --> 00:46:48,597
Crates!

770
00:46:50,766 --> 00:46:53,227
I'd been standing idle for a long time,
waiting for crates.

771
00:46:54,228 --> 00:46:55,646
Crates!

772
00:46:58,148 --> 00:46:59,566
Crates!

773
00:47:05,405 --> 00:47:06,448
Sand!

774
00:47:07,533 --> 00:47:08,367
Sandbags!

775
00:47:09,701 --> 00:47:10,702
Sandbags!

776
00:47:12,955 --> 00:47:14,373
Load up the sandbags.

777
00:47:14,915 --> 00:47:16,625
-Don't get them wet.
-I'll load them up.

778
00:47:17,626 --> 00:47:18,460
We're out of sandbags now.

779
00:47:19,294 --> 00:47:21,004
Crates!

780
00:47:22,881 --> 00:47:24,841
They were focused only on the bags.

781
00:47:26,051 --> 00:47:30,472
That's actually where
we ran into problems.

782
00:47:30,973 --> 00:47:33,976
There was a breakdown in communication.

783
00:47:39,773 --> 00:47:42,192
The other team's focusing on the crates!

784
00:47:42,276 --> 00:47:44,528
They're focusing on the crates!

785
00:47:46,780 --> 00:47:48,824
You guys, concentrate on the sandbags.

786
00:47:48,907 --> 00:47:51,243
-Isai, you're on the crates!
-Yes.

787
00:47:57,249 --> 00:47:58,750
Just bring me the crates!

788
00:48:15,851 --> 00:48:16,768
Three minutes.

789
00:48:16,852 --> 00:48:18,478
-Three minutes!
-Bring them down!

790
00:48:18,562 --> 00:48:21,607
Let's go!

791
00:48:23,942 --> 00:48:24,860
Crate!

792
00:48:24,943 --> 00:48:26,778
We can't lose this!

793
00:48:26,862 --> 00:48:28,196
Three minutes!

794
00:48:30,032 --> 00:48:35,412
The only things I paid attention to
were myself, the crates, and my teammates.

795
00:48:37,247 --> 00:48:41,418
Looking at the remaining goods,

796
00:48:41,501 --> 00:48:44,463
I could see that almost all
of our 50 kg crates were gone,

797
00:48:44,546 --> 00:48:46,423
while the other team had lots remaining.

798
00:48:47,299 --> 00:48:49,343
I was certain we were going to win.

799
00:48:51,428 --> 00:48:54,389
11 BAGS

800
00:48:54,473 --> 00:48:55,515
Are we good to go?

801
00:49:04,024 --> 00:49:06,526
We need to unload these quickly.

802
00:49:16,703 --> 00:49:19,414
I had to do something for my team.

803
00:49:21,333 --> 00:49:23,919
Once more, I gave it my all,
down to the last drop.

804
00:49:30,759 --> 00:49:32,010
Nefise, come on! Hurry!

805
00:49:36,056 --> 00:49:36,890
One minute.

806
00:49:40,894 --> 00:49:44,690
Indonesia, my native land…

807
00:49:44,773 --> 00:49:47,359
I wanted to spur my team on.

808
00:49:47,442 --> 00:49:50,654
I told them we could do it
and that we should fight for it.

809
00:49:50,737 --> 00:49:53,281
Come on, we don't have much time.
Let's try to get this up.

810
00:49:55,617 --> 00:49:56,493
Wait!

811
00:49:56,576 --> 00:49:58,078
-Push. Come on, push!
-Wait.

812
00:49:58,161 --> 00:49:59,287
Wait!

813
00:49:59,371 --> 00:50:00,706
It was just one bag,

814
00:50:00,789 --> 00:50:02,708
but I had to add to it
even though I felt like dying.

815
00:50:02,791 --> 00:50:03,625
Push.

816
00:50:05,627 --> 00:50:08,171
Yasemin, run!

817
00:50:19,224 --> 00:50:20,267
Glenn!

818
00:50:22,686 --> 00:50:23,895
Ten seconds.

819
00:50:35,574 --> 00:50:36,658
Game over.

820
00:50:40,162 --> 00:50:41,037
Stop.

821
00:50:41,121 --> 00:50:42,372
Game over.

822
00:50:48,420 --> 00:50:50,547
Hold my hands, guys.

823
00:50:52,716 --> 00:50:53,925
We did it.

824
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:56,386
We did it!

825
00:51:04,686 --> 00:51:05,937
I think we've lost.

826
00:51:07,939 --> 00:51:09,316
We might've lost.

827
00:51:10,859 --> 00:51:13,028
-How many of their crates are left?
-I don't know.

828
00:51:13,111 --> 00:51:14,237
We might've lost.

829
00:51:15,739 --> 00:51:19,493
The second quest of Physical: Asia.

830
00:51:20,118 --> 00:51:21,828
Shipwreck transportation match.

831
00:51:24,206 --> 00:51:25,248
The result of Türkiye…

832
00:51:25,332 --> 00:51:26,458
Please.

833
00:51:27,959 --> 00:51:31,254
…versus Indonesia will now be announced.

834
00:51:31,338 --> 00:51:33,465
Let's face this with an open heart.

835
00:51:37,719 --> 00:51:38,845
Indonesia.

836
00:51:46,436 --> 00:51:48,104
1,480 kg.

837
00:51:51,399 --> 00:51:52,651
We did the best we could.

838
00:51:56,988 --> 00:52:00,492
INDONESIA
16 CRATES, 34 BAGS

839
00:52:01,201 --> 00:52:02,577
Don't tell me they've won.

840
00:52:04,746 --> 00:52:05,831
Türkiye.

841
00:52:24,724 --> 00:52:28,228
TÜRKIYE
17 CRATES, 57 BAGS

842
00:52:34,693 --> 00:52:36,736
-One, two, three, Türkiye!
-One, two, three, Türkiye!

843
00:52:39,698 --> 00:52:43,577
I thank my teammates
from the bottom of my heart.

844
00:52:43,660 --> 00:52:49,624
We moved with the mindset
that we were one body, one team.

845
00:52:49,708 --> 00:52:51,626
Hey, what's that?

846
00:52:52,127 --> 00:52:55,338
Look, the Indonesians are flying out.
That's their flight.

847
00:52:55,422 --> 00:52:56,339
See you later.

848
00:52:56,423 --> 00:52:58,216
Bye-bye, Indonesia.

849
00:53:07,434 --> 00:53:08,268
It's okay.

850
00:53:09,102 --> 00:53:11,897
Honestly, it was a heartbreaking moment.

851
00:53:11,980 --> 00:53:16,318
I blamed myself for not carrying more

852
00:53:16,902 --> 00:53:19,487
and for not trying harder.

853
00:53:19,988 --> 00:53:23,825
This isn't a failure but a success
because we gave it our all.

854
00:53:23,909 --> 00:53:25,410
And that was a promise
we made to ourselves.

855
00:53:26,703 --> 00:53:29,706
-The winning team is Team Türkiye.
-Türkiye!

856
00:53:29,789 --> 00:53:31,958
-Türkiye!
-Türkiye!

857
00:53:33,835 --> 00:53:36,671
The losing team is Team Indonesia.

858
00:53:36,755 --> 00:53:38,006
Bravo, Indonesia.

859
00:53:38,089 --> 00:53:39,591
Bravo, Indonesia.

860
00:53:45,055 --> 00:53:46,306
Thanks, everyone.

861
00:53:47,182 --> 00:53:48,683
We did our best regardless of the outcome.

862
00:53:51,603 --> 00:53:55,190
Dear God, we know
that you hear our sincere prayers.

863
00:53:55,982 --> 00:53:56,983
Help us, God.

864
00:53:57,067 --> 00:54:00,153
If you give us one more chance,
we will offer you our very best,

865
00:54:00,236 --> 00:54:01,905
beyond our very best.

866
00:54:03,365 --> 00:54:04,658
I'm proud of you all.

867
00:54:04,741 --> 00:54:05,825
I'm proud of you guys.

868
00:54:05,909 --> 00:54:06,826
It's okay.

869
00:54:31,768 --> 00:54:33,395
It's hard to accept defeat.

870
00:54:34,437 --> 00:54:36,731
If I could turn back time,

871
00:54:36,815 --> 00:54:38,525
I'd wish to become stronger.

872
00:54:39,734 --> 00:54:41,569
I'm honestly so sad right now.

873
00:54:42,320 --> 00:54:45,156
I feel like we got eliminated
way too soon.

874
00:55:03,967 --> 00:55:06,344
The losing countries will be given

875
00:55:06,928 --> 00:55:10,390
one final chance
to stay in the competition.

876
00:55:16,604 --> 00:55:17,689
All four countries,

877
00:55:18,440 --> 00:55:19,441
please enter the arena.

878
00:55:20,650 --> 00:55:22,318
I wasn't expecting there to be more games.

879
00:55:25,155 --> 00:55:27,157
So this is really exciting.

880
00:55:27,240 --> 00:55:28,783
JAR
CROSSFIT ATHLETE

881
00:55:28,867 --> 00:55:31,661
Honestly, I'm thrilled to play again
because I still want to compete.

882
00:55:32,620 --> 00:55:33,580
Holy moly.

883
00:55:33,663 --> 00:55:35,498
-Come on, guys.
-Yeah, come on!

884
00:55:35,582 --> 00:55:37,459
-Bravo!
-Come on, guys!

885
00:55:42,380 --> 00:55:44,215
When we saw all four countries,

886
00:55:44,716 --> 00:55:46,968
it was going to be a combat fight…

887
00:55:47,052 --> 00:55:48,595
ROBYN
NATIONAL TEAM 400 M HURDLES ATHLETE

888
00:55:48,678 --> 00:55:50,013
…and I was nervous.

889
00:55:50,096 --> 00:55:51,598
Yeah! Come on!

890
00:55:51,681 --> 00:55:53,099
Go, Japan!

891
00:55:53,183 --> 00:55:54,225
Bring it, guys!

892
00:55:54,309 --> 00:55:55,226
It's this sand again.

893
00:55:56,519 --> 00:55:58,188
KATSUMI NAKAMURA
NATIONAL TEAM SWIMMER

894
00:55:58,271 --> 00:56:00,065
Yes, I was mad.

895
00:56:00,815 --> 00:56:03,568
We should've been up there as winners,

896
00:56:03,651 --> 00:56:06,029
looking down on the other countries.

897
00:56:06,112 --> 00:56:07,489
But at the same time,

898
00:56:07,572 --> 00:56:12,077
I wanted to show them once and for all
how strong we were and the threat we posed

899
00:56:12,160 --> 00:56:15,622
by putting on a fantastic performance.

900
00:56:16,956 --> 00:56:18,541
Let's go, Indonesia!

901
00:56:20,126 --> 00:56:23,797
All we wanted was another chance,

902
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:26,132
and that's exactly what we got.

903
00:56:26,216 --> 00:56:29,969
To be honest,
my heart was racing like crazy.

904
00:56:30,053 --> 00:56:32,055
It felt like God
had directly answered our prayers.

905
00:56:34,974 --> 00:56:36,059
We need to think ahead.

906
00:56:36,142 --> 00:56:37,602
YUSHIN OKAMI
MMA FIGHTER

907
00:56:37,685 --> 00:56:40,939
There was sand
and a water pit in front of us.

908
00:56:41,898 --> 00:56:43,900
Are all four teams going in at once?

909
00:56:44,484 --> 00:56:45,777
I saw that there was water,

910
00:56:46,277 --> 00:56:49,906
which made me think
it wasn't going to be easy.

911
00:56:51,366 --> 00:56:53,076
Damn, is this full contact?

912
00:56:53,159 --> 00:56:53,993
Definitely.

913
00:56:54,828 --> 00:56:56,746
Physical: Asia.

914
00:56:57,288 --> 00:56:59,499
The countries to be officially eliminated
will be determined…

915
00:57:05,338 --> 00:57:06,631
by the Death Match.

916
00:57:18,059 --> 00:57:19,269
Ball possession match.

917
00:57:22,480 --> 00:57:24,023
I had a feeling it would be this.

918
00:57:24,107 --> 00:57:25,316
JUSTIN COVENEY
NATIONAL TEAM RUGBY PLAYER

919
00:57:25,400 --> 00:57:27,610
A signature of the Physical: 100 series.

920
00:57:27,694 --> 00:57:29,404
It feels familiar.

921
00:57:29,487 --> 00:57:32,949
Two things sprang to mind immediately.

922
00:57:33,032 --> 00:57:33,867
PLOY
MUAY THAI COACH

923
00:57:33,950 --> 00:57:35,326
"Oh, you jerks,"

924
00:57:35,410 --> 00:57:38,163
and "Yikes."

925
00:57:38,246 --> 00:57:40,165
In the ball possession Death Match,

926
00:57:40,248 --> 00:57:43,084
two teams will compete one-on-one.

927
00:57:43,168 --> 00:57:44,669
Damn, this is going to be tough.

928
00:57:45,628 --> 00:57:46,796
-One-on-one?
-Yeah, one-on-one.

929
00:57:46,880 --> 00:57:48,131
Two countries, I guess.

930
00:57:48,214 --> 00:57:50,049
So we only compete against one of them?

931
00:57:50,133 --> 00:57:51,134
Yeah.

932
00:57:52,010 --> 00:57:54,762
To win, you must take
the ball from the center

933
00:57:55,972 --> 00:57:59,559
and score in your opponent's goal first.

934
00:58:00,435 --> 00:58:03,062
So you score on your opponent's side,
like in basketball.

935
00:58:03,146 --> 00:58:05,607
Each game will last for three minutes.

936
00:58:06,483 --> 00:58:09,068
In the event of a tie,

937
00:58:09,152 --> 00:58:13,156
a one-minute rematch will take place.

938
00:58:13,239 --> 00:58:15,325
So three minutes,
and overtime if it's a tie.

939
00:58:15,909 --> 00:58:18,453
If the playoff also ends in a tie,

940
00:58:19,287 --> 00:58:20,622
the team that gets closer

941
00:58:21,998 --> 00:58:26,044
to the opponent's goal
while holding the ball will win.

942
00:58:27,295 --> 00:58:28,963
Actually, it's like rugby.

943
00:58:29,047 --> 00:58:30,298
Yeah.

944
00:58:31,174 --> 00:58:36,554
If neither team has possession at the end,

945
00:58:37,263 --> 00:58:40,725
the playoff to decide on the winner
will be repeated.

946
00:58:40,808 --> 00:58:41,643
NONOKA OZAKI
NATIONAL TEAM WRESTLER

947
00:58:41,726 --> 00:58:44,312
So this wasn't about
holding on to the ball till the end.

948
00:58:44,395 --> 00:58:46,272
It was different from before.

949
00:58:46,356 --> 00:58:51,069
Holding onto the ball
clearly gives combat athletes an edge,

950
00:58:51,152 --> 00:58:56,533
but if you have to score a goal first,
speed becomes the priority.

951
00:58:56,616 --> 00:58:59,160
The match would be decided
right from the start.

952
00:58:59,744 --> 00:59:01,162
I was confident going into this,

953
00:59:01,246 --> 00:59:04,207
but the variable which made it challenging
was the water.

954
00:59:04,290 --> 00:59:06,000
There's no water in rugby.

955
00:59:06,084 --> 00:59:07,210
This suits me just fine.

956
00:59:07,293 --> 00:59:08,503
FINA PHILLIPE
JIUJITSU ATHLETE

957
00:59:08,586 --> 00:59:12,006
This is something I'm good at.

958
00:59:12,090 --> 00:59:14,842
Each game will consist of
a total of five rounds.

959
00:59:14,926 --> 00:59:16,344
What? Five rounds?

960
00:59:17,470 --> 00:59:22,350
Only the country
that wins three out of the five rounds

961
00:59:23,059 --> 00:59:24,352
will survive.

962
00:59:24,936 --> 00:59:27,105
It'd be good to win
the first three rounds.

963
00:59:27,981 --> 00:59:30,567
The first round will be a one-on-one.

964
00:59:31,234 --> 00:59:32,360
A one-on-one?

965
00:59:33,861 --> 00:59:36,364
The second round will be a two-on-two.

966
00:59:37,365 --> 00:59:39,325
-Oh, so it gets bigger.
-Yeah.

967
00:59:39,909 --> 00:59:42,287
The third round will be a one-on-one.

968
00:59:43,204 --> 00:59:46,124
The fourth round will be a two-on-two.

969
00:59:47,000 --> 00:59:49,502
The fifth round will be a one-on-one.

970
00:59:50,628 --> 00:59:51,713
Three one-on-ones.

971
00:59:52,297 --> 00:59:53,881
One, two, one, two, one.

972
00:59:54,882 --> 00:59:56,009
There'll be some mismatches.

973
00:59:56,092 --> 00:59:58,553
-For sure.
-Yeah, lots of mismatches.

974
00:59:58,636 --> 01:00:00,930
The two losing countries…

975
01:00:01,014 --> 01:00:03,308
Japan won't be one of them,
that's for sure.

976
01:00:03,391 --> 01:00:04,934
…will be permanently…

977
01:00:08,688 --> 01:00:12,442
eliminated from Physical: Asia.

978
01:00:12,525 --> 01:00:17,113
We need to go all out
to stay in the competition.

979
01:00:17,196 --> 01:00:18,031
LARA
CROSSFIT ATHLETE

980
01:00:18,114 --> 01:00:20,283
I'll try to finish strong
and win the quest again.

981
01:00:20,366 --> 01:00:24,120
We won't let this chance go to waste.

982
01:00:25,496 --> 01:00:26,497
Now,

983
01:00:27,874 --> 01:00:31,085
the matchups for the Death Match
will be determined.

984
01:00:31,169 --> 01:00:32,879
The matchups will decide everything.

985
01:00:32,962 --> 01:00:35,089
It's like who you match up against.

986
01:00:35,173 --> 01:00:38,468
Among the four countries
that lost in the second quest,

987
01:00:39,135 --> 01:00:44,182
the one that collected the most goods
will get to choose its opponent.

988
01:00:45,933 --> 01:00:47,935
I can't wait to find out the rankings.

989
01:00:48,019 --> 01:00:50,688
The rankings from the shipwreck
transportation match

990
01:00:51,272 --> 01:00:52,732
will now be revealed.

991
01:00:53,858 --> 01:00:56,361
-First will be the Republic of Korea,
-Please.

992
01:00:56,444 --> 01:00:57,320
Mongolia,

993
01:00:57,403 --> 01:00:58,655
Türkiye,

994
01:00:58,738 --> 01:01:01,115
and Australia's rankings.

995
01:01:08,081 --> 01:01:09,666
Korea?

996
01:01:11,042 --> 01:01:13,127
1ST PLACE: REPUBLIC OF KOREA

997
01:01:16,005 --> 01:01:16,881
Republic of Korea!

998
01:01:16,964 --> 01:01:18,466
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

999
01:01:18,966 --> 01:01:21,511
That's when the vibe
of the competition shifted again.

1000
01:01:21,594 --> 01:01:25,098
We showed them we're serious contenders
and no one can match us on stamina.

1001
01:01:25,181 --> 01:01:27,141
We've shown the full extent
of what we can do.

1002
01:01:27,642 --> 01:01:29,018
And now,

1003
01:01:30,395 --> 01:01:33,606
the rankings of the losing countries
will be revealed.

1004
01:01:37,652 --> 01:01:38,486
Damn.

1005
01:01:43,950 --> 01:01:46,369
See? Japan's tough. 1,800 kg.

1006
01:01:46,452 --> 01:01:48,413
I want them to stay.
We still need payback.

1007
01:01:48,955 --> 01:01:52,417
-Yeah, kick them out ourselves.
-Exactly. I want a proper win over them.

1008
01:01:53,126 --> 01:01:57,505
Coming in fifth was a real bummer.

1009
01:01:57,588 --> 01:02:02,552
The team needs to come together
with a renewed sense of unity

1010
01:02:02,635 --> 01:02:05,138
and an effective strategy.

1011
01:02:05,763 --> 01:02:09,600
Team Japan will be selecting its opponent

1012
01:02:09,684 --> 01:02:11,894
in the Death Match.

1013
01:02:15,565 --> 01:02:17,108
So we can pick, right?

1014
01:02:17,191 --> 01:02:18,401
Bring it!

1015
01:02:19,444 --> 01:02:20,820
This is awful.

1016
01:02:21,821 --> 01:02:24,282
Japan has four
world-class martial artists.

1017
01:02:24,365 --> 01:02:27,827
They have two
Olympic bronze medalists from Paris.

1018
01:02:27,910 --> 01:02:29,370
NONOKA OZAKI
NATIONAL TEAM WRESTLER

1019
01:02:29,454 --> 01:02:31,873
They have a Japanese MMA legend,

1020
01:02:31,956 --> 01:02:35,168
and they have a female MMA fighter
that fights in ONE Championship.

1021
01:02:35,251 --> 01:02:38,087
That's why I'm really scared
to go against them.

1022
01:02:38,171 --> 01:02:40,965
But I have no choice.
We need to play the game.

1023
01:02:41,549 --> 01:02:43,509
Thailand, the Philippines,

1024
01:02:44,051 --> 01:02:45,344
and Indonesia.

1025
01:02:45,845 --> 01:02:48,598
None of these teams is a match for us.

1026
01:02:49,182 --> 01:02:53,853
It's clear that this rule and this quest
were created for us.

1027
01:02:53,936 --> 01:02:57,315
Thailand doesn't really have
any strong players.

1028
01:02:57,398 --> 01:03:00,860
Well, they don't have any
genuinely strong players, apart from one.

1029
01:03:00,943 --> 01:03:01,903
He's right there.

1030
01:03:04,405 --> 01:03:05,323
But…

1031
01:03:06,741 --> 01:03:10,161
That entire team is avoiding eye contact.

1032
01:03:11,913 --> 01:03:13,372
I'd choose the Philippines.

1033
01:03:13,456 --> 01:03:15,208
They could choose the Philippines.

1034
01:03:15,291 --> 01:03:16,584
The Philippines?

1035
01:03:16,667 --> 01:03:17,794
I wonder how strong they are.

1036
01:03:23,341 --> 01:03:24,759
They're looking at us.

1037
01:03:25,343 --> 01:03:26,469
They're looking at us.

1038
01:03:28,596 --> 01:03:29,806
Yeah, they will pick us.

1039
01:03:31,516 --> 01:03:33,309
As long as they don't pick us, guys.

1040
01:03:33,392 --> 01:03:34,852
It's a bad matchup for us.

1041
01:03:36,813 --> 01:03:37,855
What should we do?

1042
01:03:39,273 --> 01:03:40,525
Okay.

1043
01:03:46,239 --> 01:03:47,240
Indonesia.

1044
01:03:47,907 --> 01:03:48,783
Indonesia.

1045
01:03:49,867 --> 01:03:50,785
Really?

1046
01:03:57,708 --> 01:03:58,668
Really?

1047
01:03:59,377 --> 01:04:01,045
Wow.

1048
01:04:01,128 --> 01:04:03,798
Indonesia's team leader, Igedz,

1049
01:04:03,881 --> 01:04:06,175
may be the biggest,

1050
01:04:06,259 --> 01:04:09,929
but he's not used to
physical fights or combat sports.

1051
01:04:10,012 --> 01:04:12,390
That was the main reason for our decision.

1052
01:04:13,766 --> 01:04:17,603
Look at his eyes. They're so fierce.

1053
01:04:18,187 --> 01:04:19,605
Show them your skills or not?

1054
01:04:20,189 --> 01:04:21,691
They're all the same to me.

1055
01:04:21,774 --> 01:04:25,486
It doesn't matter who you are,
what we are, or whoever you are.

1056
01:04:25,570 --> 01:04:27,530
No matter how great you are,

1057
01:04:27,613 --> 01:04:30,491
once we step into that arena,

1058
01:04:30,575 --> 01:04:32,702
we're all equal.

1059
01:04:36,914 --> 01:04:38,374
I guess I'll be facing the big man.

1060
01:04:40,084 --> 01:04:40,918
Okay.

1061
01:04:41,669 --> 01:04:45,756
When we found out we'd be facing Thailand,

1062
01:04:45,840 --> 01:04:47,758
we were quite happy,

1063
01:04:47,842 --> 01:04:52,179
because we knew we'd be able to beat them.

1064
01:04:52,263 --> 01:04:54,056
I love Pacquiao.

1065
01:04:54,140 --> 01:04:56,893
Facing off against him
is going to be very special.

1066
01:04:56,976 --> 01:05:00,730
But given his age,
he won't be that strong.

1067
01:05:08,404 --> 01:05:09,280
Let's go!

1068
01:05:09,363 --> 01:05:10,197
Nothing in the tank.

1069
01:05:10,281 --> 01:05:11,365
All or nothing.

1070
01:05:11,866 --> 01:05:12,700
Rip in, boys.

1071
01:05:12,783 --> 01:05:14,577
-Leave nothing behind, guys. Let's go.
-And girls.

1072
01:05:14,660 --> 01:05:17,330
Man, I'm just imagining
standing there myself.

1073
01:05:17,413 --> 01:05:18,831
It must suck.

1074
01:05:19,582 --> 01:05:22,251
We'll fight with everything we've got.

1075
01:05:22,335 --> 01:05:24,879
We'll win this game
and advance to the next quest.

1076
01:05:28,841 --> 01:05:32,303
We'll also do our best to win this game

1077
01:05:32,386 --> 01:05:34,096
because God is good all the time.

1078
01:05:34,764 --> 01:05:35,890
Let's go!

1079
01:05:36,807 --> 01:05:38,225
Come on, guys.

1080
01:05:38,309 --> 01:05:39,143
Let's go.

1081
01:05:39,226 --> 01:05:40,186
Dig deep.

1082
01:05:41,646 --> 01:05:42,813
Each country

1083
01:05:42,897 --> 01:05:46,776
will now select its players
for each of the five rounds.

1084
01:05:47,568 --> 01:05:49,070
Listen.

1085
01:05:49,153 --> 01:05:53,616
We need to make sure
to win this within three rounds.

1086
01:05:53,699 --> 01:05:55,201
So Sun, you go first,

1087
01:05:55,284 --> 01:05:58,287
since you can play again
in the fifth round.

1088
01:05:58,371 --> 01:05:59,372
SUPERBON
MUAY THAI FIGHTER

1089
01:05:59,455 --> 01:06:01,666
It's very important
to win the first round.

1090
01:06:01,749 --> 01:06:06,504
Taking possession of the ball,
tackling, and goal scoring,

1091
01:06:06,587 --> 01:06:08,506
all those things are right up his alley.

1092
01:06:08,589 --> 01:06:10,675
I currently play rugby
for the Thai national team.

1093
01:06:10,758 --> 01:06:12,677
My role involves tackling

1094
01:06:12,760 --> 01:06:16,639
and a lot of physical contact
with the opposing team.

1095
01:06:17,723 --> 01:06:20,142
Come at me. I'm used to this.

1096
01:06:21,143 --> 01:06:22,812
Who do you reckon
they're gonna pick first?

1097
01:06:28,442 --> 01:06:30,194
The first round of the Death Match

1098
01:06:31,028 --> 01:06:32,154
will now begin.

1099
01:06:34,115 --> 01:06:35,116
Get in, Sun.

1100
01:06:35,783 --> 01:06:37,702
We're going to win this.

1101
01:06:37,785 --> 01:06:38,828
One, two, three!

1102
01:06:38,911 --> 01:06:40,496
-Thailand, let's go!
-Let's go!

1103
01:06:47,086 --> 01:06:49,797
-The rugby guy. Starting out strong.
-Oh, it's him.

1104
01:06:50,715 --> 01:06:55,386
That guy knows how to handle a ball.

1105
01:06:56,429 --> 01:06:58,180
Come on, Philippines.

1106
01:06:58,723 --> 01:06:59,640
Let's see it!

1107
01:07:05,938 --> 01:07:08,524
MARK MUGEN
NATIONAL TEAM SAMBO ATHLETE

1108
01:07:12,278 --> 01:07:13,529
We've got the upper hand.

1109
01:07:14,363 --> 01:07:16,449
I wasn't expecting them
to lead off with him.

1110
01:07:16,532 --> 01:07:18,534
I assumed they'd also pick a rugby player.

1111
01:07:18,617 --> 01:07:20,661
When I saw who my opponent was,

1112
01:07:21,203 --> 01:07:22,496
I felt I had the advantage.

1113
01:07:22,580 --> 01:07:24,331
The first thought that came to my head is,

1114
01:07:24,415 --> 01:07:29,336
we anticipated that Mark,
being our sambo athlete, could take him,

1115
01:07:30,212 --> 01:07:31,922
coming from a grappling background.

1116
01:07:37,595 --> 01:07:40,139
I'm thinking,
"I don't wanna go back home."

1117
01:07:40,222 --> 01:07:41,932
"I'm not gonna be the first country."

1118
01:07:42,933 --> 01:07:43,934
I have the upper hand here.

1119
01:07:44,435 --> 01:07:46,395
I have to win this.

1120
01:07:47,730 --> 01:07:48,606
Ready…

1121
01:07:50,608 --> 01:07:53,027
-Go! Let's go!
-Let's go!

1122
01:08:04,497 --> 01:08:06,540
He immediately beat me to the ball.

1123
01:08:07,500 --> 01:08:09,460
He was too big, too fast.

1124
01:08:11,545 --> 01:08:13,089
Oh my god.

1125
01:08:14,715 --> 01:08:16,884
They're both going for it.

1126
01:08:20,721 --> 01:08:22,098
Can you believe that speed?

1127
01:08:23,849 --> 01:08:24,892
Get him, Mark!

1128
01:08:27,103 --> 01:08:30,523
At that point, I jumped on his back
to try to slow him down.

1129
01:08:33,109 --> 01:08:35,486
Throw him off your back.
Throw him forward!

1130
01:08:38,197 --> 01:08:41,492
But he carried me
like I was his little brother.

1131
01:08:41,575 --> 01:08:44,662
It was actually embarrassing.
He carried me and the ball

1132
01:08:44,745 --> 01:08:47,414
and continued to walk towards the goal.

1133
01:08:47,498 --> 01:08:48,332
Get up.

1134
01:08:48,415 --> 01:08:49,708
Walk. Come on, go!

1135
01:08:49,792 --> 01:08:51,127
-Let's go, Mark!
-Get him, Mark!

1136
01:08:54,964 --> 01:08:56,966
Yeah, good charge.

1137
01:08:57,049 --> 01:08:58,300
He's too strong for him.

1138
01:08:58,384 --> 01:09:01,095
He's just too strong for him.

1139
01:09:03,722 --> 01:09:05,266
He can wrestle because he's a sambo guy.

1140
01:09:05,349 --> 01:09:07,184
Yes, that's right. He's a sambo guy.

1141
01:09:10,729 --> 01:09:13,607
I had the edge on him,

1142
01:09:13,691 --> 01:09:16,569
so I just held the ball down
and didn't push myself too hard.

1143
01:09:16,652 --> 01:09:19,405
He exerted himself way more,
trying to take the ball away.

1144
01:09:19,488 --> 01:09:20,906
And that was when I realized,

1145
01:09:20,990 --> 01:09:23,409
"Okay, size matters."

1146
01:09:23,492 --> 01:09:25,953
And I know that
I have to find a way to win,

1147
01:09:27,204 --> 01:09:29,999
and look for an opening,
look for a weak spot.

1148
01:09:30,082 --> 01:09:33,085
He may be small, but he has technique.

1149
01:09:33,169 --> 01:09:37,214
He was pretty skilled at jiujitsu.

1150
01:09:38,757 --> 01:09:40,092
Two minutes.

1151
01:09:40,176 --> 01:09:43,220
Hang in there. You're doing okay,
you're closer to their goal.

1152
01:09:44,763 --> 01:09:46,807
If only he could get up right now.

1153
01:09:46,891 --> 01:09:48,893
I would reset my body.

1154
01:09:55,941 --> 01:09:57,735
-Check out his move!
-He's using a technique.

1155
01:09:59,028 --> 01:10:00,279
He's in there. He's got his arm in.

1156
01:10:00,863 --> 01:10:01,864
He's going to lose the ball.

1157
01:10:07,786 --> 01:10:09,830
He's lost it.
If he loses the ball, it's all over.

1158
01:10:09,914 --> 01:10:11,624
Grab it, Mark! You got this, Mark!

1159
01:10:11,707 --> 01:10:13,959
-Hang in there!
-Hang in there!

1160
01:10:15,211 --> 01:10:16,962
Holy moly. Submission.

1161
01:10:17,046 --> 01:10:19,048
Yeah, see?
Technique makes a huge difference.

1162
01:10:20,174 --> 01:10:22,009
Let's go, let's go!

1163
01:10:22,760 --> 01:10:24,553
Mark can wrestle.

1164
01:10:25,262 --> 01:10:27,806
Grab the ball!

1165
01:10:27,890 --> 01:10:29,350
Grab the ball. Grab the ball, yes!

1166
01:10:29,433 --> 01:10:32,269
Yes!

1167
01:10:32,353 --> 01:10:35,064
I'm trying to keep moving
and get as close to the goal as possible.

1168
01:10:35,147 --> 01:10:37,733
Thirty seconds! Hang in there, Sun!

1169
01:10:38,525 --> 01:10:40,152
Thirty seconds!

1170
01:10:40,236 --> 01:10:42,196
Sun, you've got to move out this way.

1171
01:10:43,072 --> 01:10:44,490
Sun! Don't give in!

1172
01:10:49,495 --> 01:10:50,704
He's a rugby guy, all right.

1173
01:10:50,788 --> 01:10:53,290
You can tell he's a rugby player.
He's not giving up the ball.

1174
01:11:07,471 --> 01:11:08,597
Game over.

1175
01:11:09,306 --> 01:11:11,100
He's a great rugby player for sure.

1176
01:11:14,561 --> 01:11:15,521
Great game!

1177
01:11:16,355 --> 01:11:18,524
Holy moly. What a fight, boys.

1178
01:11:19,566 --> 01:11:21,110
The game is tied.

1179
01:11:21,193 --> 01:11:23,320
The playoff will now begin.

1180
01:11:24,697 --> 01:11:28,367
Hey, in the tiebreak, if you're closest,
that's the win then, yeah?

1181
01:11:29,159 --> 01:11:31,620
This one, the one minute,
you've got to get the ball.

1182
01:11:32,413 --> 01:11:33,539
Take it off. Give it to me.

1183
01:11:33,622 --> 01:11:35,040
Take a deep breath.

1184
01:11:35,624 --> 01:11:37,126
You need to get to their side, Sun.

1185
01:11:39,169 --> 01:11:41,130
There's gonna be a rematch for one minute.

1186
01:11:42,131 --> 01:11:43,549
Don't lose the ball.

1187
01:11:44,967 --> 01:11:46,802
All my focus was on the ball.

1188
01:11:47,344 --> 01:11:48,929
I had to get hold of the ball,
no matter what.

1189
01:11:50,014 --> 01:11:52,391
I've got to get to the ball
first this time,

1190
01:11:52,474 --> 01:11:54,435
because he beat me to it last time.

1191
01:11:55,561 --> 01:11:56,520
Feed him!

1192
01:11:57,396 --> 01:11:58,939
He's hungry, man. Feed him.

1193
01:11:59,940 --> 01:12:01,984
This is a real men's fight.

1194
01:12:02,985 --> 01:12:03,861
Stand by.

1195
01:12:06,864 --> 01:12:07,698
Ready…

1196
01:12:07,781 --> 01:12:09,241
Let's go, bro. Get that ball.

1197
01:12:09,325 --> 01:12:10,492
Yup, you have this.

1198
01:12:26,342 --> 01:12:28,344
No.

1199
01:12:31,138 --> 01:12:34,433
I beat him to the ball.

1200
01:12:34,516 --> 01:12:37,770
And from that point on,
everything went according to my plan.

1201
01:12:37,853 --> 01:12:40,314
He was too big to let up

1202
01:12:40,397 --> 01:12:43,442
and to risk having him stand up again,

1203
01:12:43,525 --> 01:12:45,861
because I couldn't control him
in the first round.

1204
01:12:47,780 --> 01:12:50,699
-Sun, go over to their side!
-Go way over to their side!

1205
01:12:55,454 --> 01:12:58,499
And that if he is able to get to the ball

1206
01:12:58,582 --> 01:13:01,460
and just crawl a few feet, he's gonna win.

1207
01:13:01,543 --> 01:13:03,170
So I had to stop him in the middle.

1208
01:13:04,129 --> 01:13:05,881
-He's about to push him.
-Right.

1209
01:13:11,553 --> 01:13:12,721
Now, that's real technique.

1210
01:13:12,805 --> 01:13:15,474
Yes, yes!

1211
01:13:15,557 --> 01:13:17,184
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

1212
01:13:18,227 --> 01:13:19,186
So who wins in this case?

1213
01:13:19,269 --> 01:13:21,438
The guys on this side, the Philippines.

1214
01:13:21,522 --> 01:13:22,689
Because they're closer to that side?

1215
01:13:22,773 --> 01:13:24,400
It caught me off guard,

1216
01:13:24,483 --> 01:13:26,193
but it still wasn't clear who would win.

1217
01:13:26,276 --> 01:13:27,861
Don't give up! Come on!

1218
01:13:28,404 --> 01:13:30,114
Roll, roll, roll!

1219
01:13:30,614 --> 01:13:32,866
Come on, Sun!

1220
01:13:34,326 --> 01:13:36,245
And then once I got on top,

1221
01:13:36,787 --> 01:13:38,914
I managed to squeeze side mount position.

1222
01:13:39,998 --> 01:13:42,292
He won't be able to free himself now.

1223
01:13:42,376 --> 01:13:43,627
Twenty seconds!

1224
01:13:45,212 --> 01:13:47,256
-Go! Hold it!
-Fifteen seconds!

1225
01:13:47,339 --> 01:13:49,425
-Fifteen seconds! Hold it!
-Hold it!

1226
01:14:02,229 --> 01:14:03,480
Stop.

1227
01:14:03,564 --> 01:14:04,648
Game over.

1228
01:14:12,322 --> 01:14:14,324
The winner of the first round is…

1229
01:14:15,617 --> 01:14:16,618
Team Philippines.

1230
01:14:34,636 --> 01:14:38,307
I felt amazing, and I felt relief

1231
01:14:38,390 --> 01:14:41,143
because it was so much harder
than I thought it would be.

1232
01:14:41,226 --> 01:14:44,229
I honestly thought that
it wouldn't be as difficult as it was.

1233
01:14:44,313 --> 01:14:45,230
MARK MUGEN
NATIONAL TEAM SAMBO ATHLETE

1234
01:14:45,314 --> 01:14:46,982
SUN
NATIONAL TEAM RUGBY PLAYER

1235
01:14:47,065 --> 01:14:49,943
It's really disappointing
and a bit sad too.

1236
01:14:50,027 --> 01:14:50,861
But…

1237
01:14:51,904 --> 01:14:53,238
I have to accept the result.

1238
01:15:01,830 --> 01:15:03,624
Physical: Asia.

1239
01:15:04,458 --> 01:15:06,335
The second round of the Death Match.

1240
01:15:07,628 --> 01:15:09,963
-It's two players this time, right?
-Yeah.

1241
01:15:10,047 --> 01:15:11,715
I think the two-on-two
will be more exciting.

1242
01:15:12,216 --> 01:15:14,801
There'll be plenty of times

1243
01:15:15,385 --> 01:15:17,971
when someone grabs the ball and runs,
then someone else chases them.

1244
01:15:19,598 --> 01:15:21,391
I wonder which two it'll be.

1245
01:15:22,351 --> 01:15:25,562
The match, we do our… Men, both men?

1246
01:15:25,646 --> 01:15:26,939
-Yup.
-Yeah? Okay.

1247
01:15:27,022 --> 01:15:28,273
-Speed.
-Yeah.

1248
01:15:28,357 --> 01:15:30,484
Guys, the ball is only 3 kilos.

1249
01:15:30,567 --> 01:15:31,860
And then I block the other one.

1250
01:15:31,944 --> 01:15:33,278
When we get the ball,

1251
01:15:33,362 --> 01:15:36,949
make sure that you get closer to our goal.

1252
01:15:37,032 --> 01:15:38,367
Yes, the other…

1253
01:15:38,450 --> 01:15:40,244
Yeah, the other side.

1254
01:15:40,327 --> 01:15:41,954
It is a good pair because…

1255
01:15:42,037 --> 01:15:42,871
RAY
STRONGMAN

1256
01:15:42,955 --> 01:15:46,083
…I have the strength,
and Manny Pacquiao has the speed.

1257
01:15:46,166 --> 01:15:49,002
When they revealed the rankings…

1258
01:15:49,086 --> 01:15:50,754
MANNY PACQUIAO
BOXER

1259
01:15:50,837 --> 01:15:54,550
…it was disappointing to come last
in eighth place.

1260
01:15:56,260 --> 01:15:57,344
But we told ourselves

1261
01:15:57,427 --> 01:16:00,264
that it was okay
because we would redeem ourselves.

1262
01:16:00,347 --> 01:16:05,060
We would do our absolute best to win
and redeem ourselves.

1263
01:16:08,146 --> 01:16:10,774
It looks like the big man, Pacquiao,
is playing in the second round.

1264
01:16:11,483 --> 01:16:12,985
It's you and James, right?

1265
01:16:14,528 --> 01:16:17,864
Since we have to
take possession of the ball…

1266
01:16:17,948 --> 01:16:18,949
SUPERBON
MUAY THAI FIGHTER

1267
01:16:19,032 --> 01:16:21,118
…we chose James and myself
for our strength and size.

1268
01:16:21,201 --> 01:16:26,415
We were confident that James and I
would win the second round.

1269
01:16:26,498 --> 01:16:27,374
JAMES RUSAMEEKAE
FORMER VOLLEYBALL PLAYER

1270
01:16:27,457 --> 01:16:29,084
Contestants of the second round,

1271
01:16:29,167 --> 01:16:31,336
please enter the arena.

1272
01:16:39,136 --> 01:16:41,221
Superbon!

1273
01:16:41,847 --> 01:16:43,140
He's a Muay Thai fighter, right?

1274
01:16:43,807 --> 01:16:46,768
Yeah, a Muay Thai fighter.

1275
01:16:49,021 --> 01:16:49,855
This team's really strong.

1276
01:16:49,938 --> 01:16:51,690
How would you even fight that strongman?

1277
01:16:52,608 --> 01:16:53,609
He's an absolute unit.

1278
01:16:56,320 --> 01:16:57,821
Manny!

1279
01:17:01,783 --> 01:17:03,076
Represent!

1280
01:17:04,369 --> 01:17:05,787
Come on, Manny!

1281
01:17:07,205 --> 01:17:08,123
Nice, Manny.

1282
01:17:08,206 --> 01:17:09,124
Come on, guys.

1283
01:17:09,666 --> 01:17:10,500
Let's go.

1284
01:17:10,584 --> 01:17:12,544
Dig deep. Come on!

1285
01:17:13,545 --> 01:17:15,672
It's boxer versus kickboxer.

1286
01:17:15,756 --> 01:17:16,840
Boxing versus Muay Thai.

1287
01:17:19,760 --> 01:17:21,011
I wonder how it'll go down.

1288
01:17:22,346 --> 01:17:27,184
I'm pumped we got the Philippines
because it means facing Pacquiao.

1289
01:17:27,267 --> 01:17:31,647
I really want to beat a top fighter.

1290
01:17:31,730 --> 01:17:34,316
I've got to take down Pacquiao.

1291
01:17:38,487 --> 01:17:39,488
Is he tying his hair?

1292
01:17:40,489 --> 01:17:42,407
He's showing a different side of himself.

1293
01:17:43,075 --> 01:17:44,993
I wanna see him get aggressive.
I wanna see if he can get aggressive.

1294
01:17:45,077 --> 01:17:46,953
I wanna see him like, get the sass out.

